      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To compute the determinant of the 2x2 matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} 7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{vmatrix}\\), we use the formula for the determinant of a 2x2 matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix}\\), which is given by \\(ad - bc\\).\n\nHere, the elements of the matrix are:\n\\[ a = 7, \\quad b = 3, \\quad c = -1, \\quad d = 2. \\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the determinant formula, we get:\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} 7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{vmatrix} = (7)(2) - (3)(-1).\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplications:\n\\[\n(7)(2) = 14,\n\\]\n\\[\n(3)(-1) = -3.\n\\]\n\nNext, we subtract the second product from the first:\n\\[\n14 - (-3) = 14 + 3 = 17.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the determinant of the matrix is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{17}.\n\\]",
