      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To compute the determinant of a 2x2 matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix}\\), we use the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{det} = ad - bc\n\\]\nFor the given matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} 7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{vmatrix}\\), we identify the elements as follows:\n\\[\na = 7, \\quad b = 3, \\quad c = -1, \\quad d = 2\n\\]\nNow, we substitute these values into the determinant formula:\n\\[\n\\text{det} = (7 \\cdot 2) - (3 \\cdot -1)\n\\]\nFirst, we calculate the product \\(7 \\cdot 2\\):\n\\[\n7 \\cdot 2 = 14\n\\]\nNext, we calculate the product \\(3 \\cdot -1\\):\n\\[\n3 \\cdot -1 = -3\n\\]\nNow, we substitute these results back into the determinant formula:\n\\[\n\\text{det} = 14 - (-3)\n\\]\nSubtracting a negative number is equivalent to adding the positive counterpart:\n\\[\n14 - (-3) = 14 + 3 = 17\n\\]\nTherefore, the determinant of the matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} 7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{vmatrix}\\) is \\(\\boxed{17}\\).",
